{"orgCode":"4100","name":"State Council on Developmental Disabilities","agencyCode":"4000","agencyName":"Health and Human Services","description":"Through programs, projects, and activities consistent with the federal Developmental Disabilities Act and the California Lanterman Developmental Disabilities Services Act, the State Council on Developmental Disabilities is responsible for engaging in advocacy, capacity building, and systems change activities that promote self-determination, independence, productivity, and inclusion in all aspects of community life for Californians with developmental disabilities and their families.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":11466,"cy":9853,"by":11304},"positions":{"py":71.2,"cy":81,"by":81},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":6080,"cy":6726,"by":7573}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/4000/4100","kind":"department","name":"State Council on Developmental Disabilities","code":"4100","amounts":{"py":11466,"cy":9853,"by":11304},"positions":{"py":71.2,"cy":81,"by":81},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":3801,"cy":959,"by":2400},"federal":{"py":7665,"cy":8894,"by":8904}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4100/3800","kind":"program","name":"State Council Planning and Administration","code":"3800","amounts":{"py":2466,"cy":2869,"by":2875},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":2466,"cy":2869,"by":2875}},"positions":{"py":21,"cy":19.5,"by":19.5},"description":"3800 - STATE COUNCIL PLANNING AND ADMINISTRATION\n\nThe Council is responsible for developing and implementing a State Plan containing goals, objectives, activities, and projected outcomes designed to improve and enhance the availability and quality of services and supports to individuals with developmental disabilities and their families. The appointed Council members engage in policy planning to ensure system coordination, barrier removal, monitoring, and evaluation. Additionally, Council staff promote implementation of the regional center Self-Determination Program and appoint representatives to protect the civil rights of individuals served by regional centers who have no legally appointed representative to assist them in making choices and decisions.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2466,"cy":2869,"by":3605}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4100/3800/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":2466,"cy":2869,"by":2875},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":2466,"cy":2869,"by":2875}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2466,"cy":2869,"by":2875}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/4000/4100/3800/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":730},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":730}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":730}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":730}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4100/3805","kind":"program","name":"Community Program Development","code":"3805","amounts":{"py":283,"cy":260,"by":260},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":283,"cy":260,"by":260}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"description":"3805 - COMMUNITY PROGRAM DEVELOPMENT\n\nThe Council administers grants to community-based organizations that fund new and innovative community program development projects to implement State Plan objectives and improve and enhance services for individuals with developmental disabilities and their families.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":283,"cy":260,"by":260}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4100/3805/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":283,"cy":260,"by":260},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":283,"cy":260,"by":260}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":283,"cy":260,"by":260}}}}]},{"id":"exp/4000/4100/3810","kind":"program","name":"Regional Offices and Regional Advisory Committees","code":"3810","amounts":{"py":8717,"cy":6724,"by":8169},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":3801,"cy":959,"by":2400},"federal":{"py":4916,"cy":5765,"by":5769}},"positions":{"py":50.2,"cy":61.5,"by":61.5},"description":"3810 - REGIONAL OFFICES AND REGIONAL ADVISORY COMMITTEES\n\nTwelve Regional Offices and Regional Advisory Committees provide programmatic support to assist with advocacy, capacity building, systems change, and implementation of State Plan objectives in Council Regions throughout California. These offices and advisory committees provide information and data to the Council to assess regional needs and implementation of the State Plan for inclusion in reports to the federal government and the Legislature. These offices also carry out direct service supports for emergency preparation and responses.\n\nIn addition to implementation of State Plan activities, Regional Office staff support the following activities to improve and enhance the availability and quality of services for regional center consumers and residents of state developmental centers:\n\n• Clients' rights advocacy services to ensure that laws, regulations, and policies pertaining to the rights of persons with developmental disabilities are observed.\n\n• Quality Assessments for individuals who receive community residential services and support.\n\n• Other efforts and projects related to self-determination and supported decision-making.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":14797,"cy":13450,"by":15012}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4100/3810/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":3801,"cy":959,"by":2400},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":3801,"cy":959,"by":2400}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":3801,"cy":959,"by":2400}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4100/3810/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":4916,"cy":5765,"by":5769},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":4916,"cy":5765,"by":5769}},"extra":{"